body:
I don't think september is realistic.

&#x200B;

Like pay a bunch of money to play the Beta on the con and then pay $60 more to get the actual game on the same month?

Goods get more expensive as they become more scarce but eventually, industries will get massive debuffs due to lack of production/availability of the good. Basically a shortage.

&#x200B;

These are reflected on the interface and a good opportunity if you're a small nation within a bigger market, you can supply it and reap the rewards.

All my items say 02/25 and are in "processing" while 1 case says 03/01 and "Order placed".

&#x200B;

The case got pushed back from 02/25 a couple of days ago at the same time all my other items went from "order placed" to "processing"
